+# Next native increment: document → dedicated worker
+
+Status: isolated design dependency, **not implemented or verified**.
+`nativeCausalIdentity` remains unsupported. No timestamps, message payloads, hashes,
+page wrappers or matching heuristics are used to correlate messages.
+
+Before implementation, obtain a pinned, security-maintained Gecko checkout and a
+buildable desktop host. Inspect its actual document/worker postMessage cloning,
+enqueue, dispatch and cancellation paths. Verify whether an upstream actor exposes
+the needed native operation identity. No actor name or source symbol is assumed here.
+If absent, review a minimal native hook against that exact revision; document the
+line-level source, thread ownership, security review and collector shutdown path.
+
+Carry a native operation identity (producer epoch + monotonic native counter) with
+the internal message operation, outside webpage-visible payload serialization.
+Emit immutable records linked by that identity for:
+
+1. `prepared`: serialization/preparation completed or failed, document and worker identities.
+2. `enqueue-result`: accepted/rejected; rejection cannot imply eventual delivery.
+3. `dispatch-start`: worker begins delivering the corresponding event.
+4. `dispatch-end`: synchronous dispatch returned, including exception disposition.
+5. `delivery-error`: a specific failed delivery with its native operation ID.
+6. `cancelled`: lifecycle cancellation with a verified native reason.
+
+Absent phases remain absent, with coverage gaps. `dispatch-end` does not mean promises,
+network requests or any other asynchronous work launched by listeners has completed.
+No extension to shared workers, service workers, MessagePorts or arbitrary worker
+network activity belongs in this increment.
+
+Tests must force enqueue failure, worker termination before dispatch, throwing
+listeners, navigation, collector detach and transport loss. Compare instrumented
+and uninstrumented message semantics. Gate on no leaks, no webpage payload change,
+and continued broker controls during stalled content. Keep collector code behind
+explicit capabilities and pinned-revision regression tests. Engine security updates
+take precedence over retaining an obsolete hook; disable unsupported tracing until
+the updated revision is revalidated.
